/* Touch-trace diagnostic overlay.
 *
 * reads stays at the production 16. An earlier revision of this file forced
 * reads=<1> to expose the per-conversion settling curve, and the board then
 * reported NO touch events at all across two 100 s captures: with a single
 * unaveraged round, the driver's z (Z1 + 4096 - Z2) is one noisy sample
 * against z-threshold=400, so `pressed` never asserts and nothing is reported.
 *
 * It was also the wrong experiment. The transient being measured spans the
 * first few REPORTS after pen-down, not the reads inside one report, so the
 * production value is what should be characterised.
 *
 * The file is kept (rather than dropped) so the trace build keeps an explicit,
 * documented DTS state -- DTS is last-one-wins here and silence is how the
 * stray reads=<3> went unnoticed for days.
 */
&xpt2046 {
	reads = <16>;
};
